-- R41 - OPEN-POSITION SWEEP
-- Source: thread "Upgrade Fable Takeaways from Opus gaps", owner's ask of 27 Nov 2026; month comparison 27 Oct to 27 Nov.
-- Proposed 27 Nov 2026 and put in force early by single-statement UPDATE the same day (print and input additions only). "revert R41" removes it.
-- Early in force: update dash.rules set status='in_force', decided_at=now(), apply_after=now() where rid='R41';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "OPEN-POSITION SWEEP: every open card, sleeve theme and open question gets a daily search for official action, crowd extremes, dated releases and FX option expiries on its underlying, printed on its review line", "body": "OPEN-POSITION SWEEP (owner's ask of 27 Nov 2026 to make Fable comprehensive enough to stand alone; from a month's comparison of the Fable edition with the Opus, Gemini and ChatGPT editions of the same mornings, 27 Oct to 27 Nov).\n\n1. WHAT. Before the card reviews are written, for every open card (thematic, tactical, hedge, convexity), every open DURABLE THEMES sleeve position and every open question, the run searches today's inputs (all feeds and their copies, DESK INPUT and carried DESK INPUT, the Grok crowding check, the Exa sweep under R40, the market pack, the positioning table, the extremes file) for four things on that underlying, and when the inputs carry nothing on (a) it makes one web search for the central bank, finance ministry or regulator of that market over the last 24 hours (at most eight such searches in all, open cards first, then sleeve themes; questions use the inputs only; inside the completeness sweep's time box, never delaying the 08:15 landing):\n(a) OFFICIAL: intervention (spot, NDF/DNDF, bond buying), verbal warnings, FX, capital-flow or short-sale rules, liquidity operations, debt-issuance or budget decisions that change supply, policy decisions, minutes or speeches by voters;\n(b) CROWD AND FLOW: a positioning reading at a 3-year extreme (5th percentile or below, 95th or above: CFTC, DTCC option notional or risk reversals, retail FX, exchange foreign flows, bond futures) or a flow print of record size;\n(c) NEXT: every scheduled release, auction or official data release on that market before the card's next review or the question's resolution, with date, SGT time, consensus and prior;\n(d) EXPIRIES (cash FX and FX option cards, and any FX expression printed as a candidate): FX option expiries of USD 1bn or more within 1% of spot over the next five sessions, and barrier or strike clusters the feeds report.\n\n2. PRINT. Each card's review line, each sleeve theme's for/against lines and each open question's line carries one line: \"SWEEP: official <item, source> · crowd <item> · next <date event cons/prior> · expiries <strike size date>\", with \"none\" in any empty slot, or \"SWEEP: nothing new (<n> sources checked)\". An item that cuts against the position is always printed, even when it does not change the verdict. An official action against a card forces a review verdict (intact, weakened or broken) that names it. A question whose RULE names a source is checked at that source first and resolves the day the source prints.\n\n3. LIMITS. Evidence only: a sweep item never opens, sizes or closes a card by itself. An official item is confirmed by R32's route before it changes a verdict or p; until then it prints with \"[unconfirmed]\". A number from another Takeaways edition (Opus, Gemini, ChatGPT, Pipeline) is a lead only and is never used until checked at its own source. Never trimmed under R33 for open cards; for sleeve themes and questions, R33 may move the line to the overflow file.\n\n4. FOOTER. \"Open-position sweep: <n> positions, <m> items (<k> against), web searches <w>\".", "rationale": "Month comparison (project files fable_gap_review/, 27 Oct to 27 Nov 2026): the most frequent material Fable gap was evidence on an underlying it already held that a peer edition carried and the card review ignored: central bank intervention and bond-sale flows against an open long USD-Asia card, finance ministry warnings and a barrier cluster against an open yen card, a 3-year CFTC extreme and stale rate pricing against a sleeve position, a margin rule against another sleeve position, a regulator probe bearing on an open question, and question sources named in the rule but read a day late. Fable's errors were omissions, not wrong facts, so the fix is a forced search per position. The prompts are at their byte cap, so this goes in as a rule.", "evidence": "Project files fable_gap_review/gaps_w1..w5.tsv and gaps_d27nov.tsv; summaries per week.", "revert_if": "Revert if, over three weeks, the sweep lines add nothing a card review did not already carry, or the email goes over R33's budget on two mornings because of them.", "review_due": "2026-12-18", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
